============================================================================================
HOW TO READ THIS
============================================================================================
  static_now is the existing static_arb with one-way costs. If it is
  positive here and negative in the round-trip script, the entire
  difference is the exit leg -- a cost-structure result, not a
  forecasting one, and it must not be reported as the model working.

  The model's contribution is ONLY the model_timed - random_timed row.
  Everything else differs in more than the forecast.

  A basket held to settlement captures |dev| whatever the path, so the
  model is not predicting convergence -- it is predicting whether
  waiting one step buys a wider dislocation. That is the entire claim
  this script can support.

  If maker execution shows a net credit, check the unfilled count and
  the capital-lockup line before believing it. Whelan measured Kalshi
  makers at -9.64% on average, so a model that shows makers earning
  the spread with no adverse selection is modelling something easier
  than the real venue.
